From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd: the interrupt loop ends on a failed status read

A cable replug during a suspend leaves the codec unreadable at the wake. The loop ignored its status
reads' errors and went on with their old values, spinning in the SoundWire interrupt thread at FIFO
priority: the codec's interrupt was disabled after 100000 rounds, USB stayed down, and a task waiting
for another interrupt thread ended in a hung task panic.
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-common.c
@@ -130,9 +130,14 @@

 	do {
 		handle_nested_irq(irq_find_mapping(slave_irq, 0));
-		regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status0, &sts1);
-		regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status1, &sts2);
-		regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status2, &sts3);
+		/*
+		 * A failed read says nothing about the status, and the status can't clear while the
+		 * codec is unreachable: stay here and this thread starves what runs behind it.
+		 */
+		if (regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status0, &sts1) ||
+		    regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status1, &sts2) ||
+		    regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status2, &sts3))
+			break;

 	} while (sts1 || sts2 || sts3);

